 "state_profile": {
  "voting_summary": "Arizona is functionally a vote-by-mail state: 85% of its 2024 vote arrived as early (mail) ballots. Polls close at 9 p.m. Eastern; pre-processed early ballots are released first in a large batch, followed by election day precincts overnight. Mail dropped off on election day ('late earlies') requires days of signature verification, famously stretching Maricopa County's count across a week or more. Election day voting ran R+26 versus R+2 for early ballots, so Republicans gain overnight and close races hang on the late-early count for days.",
